From: OpenHarmony Third-Party Adaptation <noreply@openharmony.io>
Subject: [PATCH] guard TCGETA/TCSETA redefinitions for musl (OHOS)

musl does not provide <termio.h> (removed in musl 1.1.15+, and never
present on OHOS), and its <bits/ioctl.h> already defines TCGETA/TCSETA
as int ioctls.  The unconditional

    #define TCGETA TIOCGETA
    #define TCSETA TIOCSETA

in src/run.c therefore references TIOCGETA/TIOCSETA, which do not exist
under musl, producing (clang, OHOS armv8):

    src/run.c:76:11: error: use of undeclared identifier 'TIOCGETA'
    src/run.c:76:11: error: use of undeclared identifier 'TIOCSETA'

Guard both redefinitions with #ifndef so glibc keeps its TIOCGETA/
TIOCSETA based definitions while musl (OHOS) uses its native
TCGETA/TCSETA values.

Note: the diff body below is a zero-context (-U0) hunk so that the
patch file itself contains no "space before tab" lines (the guarded
region is surrounded by tab-indented and blank context lines whose
diff markers would otherwise trip whitespace checks).  Apply with
`git apply --unidiff-zero -p1` or let Conan (patch_ng) apply it; both
engines match the hunk by line number and content.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OHOS/musl specific]

---
 src/run.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/run.c b/src/run.c
index b89d959..d242d15 100644
--- a/src/run.c
+++ b/src/run.c
@@ -25,2 +25,7 @@
-	#define TCGETA TIOCGETA
-	#define TCSETA TIOCSETA
+	// musl (OHOS) already defines TCGETA/TCSETA in bits/ioctl.h
+	#ifndef TCGETA
+	#define TCGETA TIOCGETA
+	#endif
+	#ifndef TCSETA
+	#define TCSETA TIOCSETA
+	#endif
